## Summary

After #7575 (commit b9a0994c1c, "Support more types in decoupled lookback fastpath"), `cub::DeviceScan::InclusiveSum` fails to compile for types that are marked as primitive via `cub::NumericTraits` but have `sizeof(T) >= 16`, such as `thrust::complex<double>`.

## Root cause

#7575 changed the default template parameter of `ScanTileState` to include `is_primitive<T>` in the `SingleWord` condition:

```cpp
// single_pass_scan_operators.cuh, line ~657
bool SingleWord = detail::is_primitive<T>::value
                   || ::cuda::std::is_trivially_copyable_v<T>
                   && sizeof(T) < detail::largest_atomic_message_size
```

Due to C++ operator precedence (`&&` binds tighter than `||`), this evaluates as:

```cpp
is_primitive<T>::value || (is_trivially_copyable_v<T> && sizeof(T) < 16)
```

When `is_primitive<T>::value` is `true`, `SingleWord` is unconditionally `true` regardless of `sizeof(T)`. This selects the `ScanTileState<T, true>` specialization, which then hits:

```cpp
static_assert(sizeof(TileDescriptor) <= detail::largest_atomic_message_size);
```

For `thrust::complex<double>` (`sizeof == 16`), `TileDescriptor = {StatusWord, T}` exceeds 16 bytes.

## Who is affected

Projects like [CuPy](https://github.com/cupy/cupy) specialize `cub::NumericTraits` for complex types to enable CUB device algorithms:

```cpp
template <>
struct NumericTraits<thrust::complex<double>>
    : BaseTraits<FLOATING_POINT, true, unsigned long long,
                 thrust::complex<double>> {};
```

The second `BaseTraits` template parameter (`true`) marks the type as "primitive". This pattern worked on all prior CCCL releases and breaks after #7575.

## Minimal reproducer

```cpp
#include <thrust/complex.h>
#include <cuda/std/limits>

// Trait specializations to enable CUB device algorithms on complex types
// (same pattern used by CuPy)
namespace cuda {
namespace std {
template <>
class numeric_limits<thrust::complex<double>> {
  public:
    static __host__ __device__ thrust::complex<double> max() noexcept {
        return thrust::complex<double>(
            cuda::std::numeric_limits<double>::max(),
            cuda::std::numeric_limits<double>::max());
    }
    static __host__ __device__ thrust::complex<double> lowest() noexcept {
        return thrust::complex<double>(
            -cuda::std::numeric_limits<double>::max(),
            -cuda::std::numeric_limits<double>::max());
    }
    static constexpr bool is_specialized = true;
};
}  // namespace std
template <>
inline constexpr bool is_floating_point_v<thrust::complex<double>> = true;
}  // namespace cuda

#include <cub/util_type.cuh>
using namespace cub;
template <>
struct NumericTraits<thrust::complex<double>>
    : BaseTraits<FLOATING_POINT, true, unsigned long long,
                 thrust::complex<double>> {};

#include <cub/device/device_scan.cuh>
#include <cstdio>

int main() {
    using T = thrust::complex<double>;
    const int n = 1024;
    T* d_in = nullptr;
    T* d_out = nullptr;
    void* d_tmp = nullptr;
    size_t tmp_bytes = 0;

    cudaMalloc(&d_in, n * sizeof(T));
    cudaMalloc(&d_out, n * sizeof(T));

    // This triggers the static_assert failure
    auto err = cub::DeviceScan::InclusiveSum(
        d_tmp, tmp_bytes, d_in, d_out, n);

    printf("err = %d\n", (int)err);
    cudaFree(d_in);
    cudaFree(d_out);
    return 0;
}
```

Compile with:
```
nvcc --std=c++17 --expt-relaxed-constexpr \
  -I <cccl>/cub -I <cccl>/thrust -I <cccl>/libcudacxx/include \
  cccl_scan_complex_repro.cu
```

Error:
```
single_pass_scan_operators.cuh(693): error: static assertion failed
    static_assert(sizeof(TileDescriptor) <= detail::largest_atomic_message_size);
```

## Suggested fix

The `SingleWord` condition should ensure the size check applies to both `is_primitive` and `is_trivially_copyable` types. For example:

```cpp
bool SingleWord = (detail::is_primitive<T>::value
                   || ::cuda::std::is_trivially_copyable_v<T>)
                   && sizeof(T) < detail::largest_atomic_message_size
```

Or alternatively, add `sizeof(T) < detail::largest_atomic_message_size` to the `is_primitive` branch explicitly.

